319 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 179 0 R
/E (Forking creates a complete copy of a fragment that breaks away from its original lineage. Unlike branching, which stays within the same creative thread, a fork establishes a new, parallel path often in a different session. This is ideal when an idea needs to be reimagined without constraints, allowing for a fresh direction while still retaining access to the original source.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
